• Use the object Chart 
  for presenting current data and results of the simulation run.
• Use the object Checkbox 
  for toggling between the states on and off, for toggling operating modes,
etc.
• Use the object Comment 
  for showing explanatory notes which you added to your simulation model.
• Use the object CostAnalyzer 
  for analyzing costs that the individual machines and the Worker cause.
• Use the object Dialog 
  for designing a dialog box for an object which is similar to the built-in dialog
boxes.
• Use the object Display 
  for presenting current data and results of the simulation run.
• Use the object DropDownList 
  for showing a drop-down list in the Frame. When you select one of the
items, it executes the action which you programmed in the control.
• Use the object GanttChart 
  for showing the chronological sequence of activities as bars on the time
axis.
• Use the object HtmlReport 
  for presenting current data and results of the simulation run in a report
that you can share with co-workers and customers.
• Use the object SankeyDiagram 
  for visualizing the Sankey flows of parts as well as Sankey flows of
Workers, who walk freely within the area or walk on FootPaths.
Comment
Comment [object]
Use the object Comment for showing explanatory notes which you added to your simulation model.
Image
Description
A comment helps you and your colleagues to better understand the intentions behind your model and
how it is supposed to work.
You can access it like you do any other object, be aware though that the Comment usually is not involved
in the simulation itself. Select Options > Show Comments on the View ribbon tab of the Frame or click
 to display all Comment objects, which you inserted into that Frame. Plant Simulation displays the text
in the Frame window which you entered under Display > Text.
Comment
11-4554 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To open a window that only shows the comment you entered, without formatting and editing options,
click the Comment object with the right mouse button and select Open Comment Window on the context
menu.
To show a tooltip with information about the Comment, hover with the mouse over it.
To change the length of the graphic and the anchor points of the Comment, click Show Manipulators
 on the Edit ribbon tab or press M on the keyboard.
Add the Object to the Simulation Model
To add the object Comment to your simulation model, click 
  Manage Class Library > Basic Objects >
UserInterface > Comment on the Home ribbon tab.
See also
Add Text and Display Boards
Dialog Box of the Comment
Dialog Box of the Comment
Double-click the icon of the Comment, which you inserted into a Frame, to open its dialog box.
Edit Simulation Properties
To make the dialog box larger or smaller, grab any of its sides or corners, and drag the mouse.
Dialog Box of the Comment
Plant Simulation Help 11-4555
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To open a window that only shows the comment you entered, without formatting and editing options,
click the Comment object with the right mouse button and select Open Comment Window on the context
menu.
Plant Simulation opens the comment window with the size that the tab Comment in the dialog box had,
when you entered the comment and with the formatting you applied.
To close the comment window, click Close 
  in the title bar.
Edit Animation Properties
To edit the 3D properties of the object in the dialog box Edit 3D Properties:
• Click the button 
  Edit 3D Properties in the lower left corner of the simulation properties dialog box.
• Select the object in the model and press the spacebar.
To manipulate the graphic of the object, click Show Manipulators on the Edit ribbon tab or press M on the
keyboard.
Dialog Box of the Comment
11-4556 Plant Simulation Help
